<Layout title="Ratings privacy | Legacy of Goku Hub"><main id="main" class="container"><h1>Ratings privacy</h1><p>No account or sign-in is required. Your browser generates a random voting credential and stores it locally. The server stores only its cryptographic hash, your current score, and project ID. Public visitors see only averages and vote counts. We do not collect your name, email, GitHub identity, or browser fingerprint.</p><p>Anyone with your voting credential can change its ratings. Do not share it. Returning to the same browser lets you change or remove a rating. Clearing browser data, using another browser, or browsing privately may create another identity and lose access to previous votes. Anonymous voting cannot guarantee one vote per human.</p><p>Activate the already-selected Dragon Ball on a project again to remove your rating. If the credential is lost, we cannot prove which vote was yours. Maintainers can exclude fraudulent ratings from aggregates. Short-lived salted network hashes help rate-limit abuse; raw IP addresses are not stored in the database. Cloudflare processes network requests under its own privacy policy.</p><p>Votes remain until removed, excluded, or their project is removed. Rate-limit records expire after two minutes and are cleaned every ten minutes. Private exports and deletion markers are retained for at most seven days. Maintainers reapply deletion and fraud exclusions before recovery; if the current ledger is unavailable, voting stays unavailable rather than restoring deleted votes. No raw voter records or credentials are published with the directory.</p><a href="/">Back to projects</a></main></Layout>

